<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- URLs match the canonicals in each page's head, which means no trailing
     slash and no .html — server.js strips both. A sitemap that disagrees with
     the canonical tag is worse than no sitemap. /get-started, /start and
     /signup are deliberately absent: each 307s to the app's sign-up, and
     listing a redirect is the disagreement this comment warns about. So is
     /start-scroll, which nothing links and which canonicalises elsewhere.

     This file held exactly one entry — https://fuime.com/ — for as long as
     server.js's CLOSED set bounced every other page to the front door. The
     site opened on 2026-09-14 and they came back in the same commit that
     emptied it, as the previous version of this comment promised they would.

     test/server.test.mjs fetches every <loc> below and fails on anything that
     does not answer 200, so this list cannot rot into pointing at a 404. -->
